# oracle: fix lb/fluid with the Gaussian noise (D3Q15, trilinear stencil) with lb/viscous, rigid molecules and fix lb/momentum (examples/PACKAGES/latboltz/microrheology/in.microrheology, cut down: dx 4.0 instead of 1.2, 100 steps, lb/momentum every 100 steps instead of 50000 so that it acts in the short run). Measured with native (b332f28 built with -D PKG_LATBOLTZ=on): thermo (particle positions) 1.7e-11 relative; per-atom velocities and forces 2.6e-4 relative (atomrel). The noise draws use glibc log(), which differs from V8 Math.log by one ulp in about 7% of draws, and the coupled dynamics amplify that; the first step alone agrees to 1e-11 per atom (w132lb_noise1), and the fluid without particles agrees to 1e-16.
# oracle-inputs: w132lb_microrheology.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-10 atomrel=1e-3
units           nano
dimension       3
boundary        p p p
atom_style      molecular
read_data       w132lb_microrheology.data
neighbor        0.3 bin
neigh_modify    delay 0 every 1
neigh_modify    exclude type 2 2
neigh_modify    exclude type 2 1
comm_modify     cutoff 2.5
pair_style      lj/cut 5.88
pair_coeff      * * 0.0 0.0 5.88
pair_coeff      1 1 100.0 5.238484463 5.88
pair_modify     shift yes
mass            * 0.0002398
timestep        0.00025
group           ForceAtoms type 1
group           FluidAtoms type 2
fix             1 FluidAtoms lb/fluid 1 1.0 0.0009982071 dx 4.0 stencil 2 noise 300.0 2762
fix             2 FluidAtoms lb/viscous
fix             3 all rigid molecule
fix             4 all lb/momentum 100 linear 1 1 1
variable        x1 equal x[1]
variable        y1 equal y[1]
variable        z1 equal z[1]
variable        x2 equal x[242]
variable        y2 equal y[242]
variable        z2 equal z[242]
thermo_style    custom step v_x1 v_y1 v_z1 v_x2 v_y2 v_z2
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          20
run             100
